{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>תשלח, עד ים</b> — in length, from the Sea of Reeds to the sea of the Philistines." "<b>ואל נהר</b> — the Euphrates River, in width." "<b>יונקותיה</b> — the branches are the small ones, resembling sucklings. And it is possible that the meaning of \"the mountains and the cedars\" is that Israel were the high mountains and the forests," "<b>וטעם ארזי אל</b> — like the expression: כהררי אל."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:33.957809738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}